  invited
  external
  shadow

  @@map("entity_type")
}

// ---- Off-system ("external") teachers -------------------------------------
//
// A center may run on the platform while one of its teachers refuses to (or
// keeps their own system). The center still needs a 100% complete picture of
// those students, lessons and money, so the center's STAFF enter those records
// by hand.
//
// An external teacher IS a normal `users` row (role=teacher, status='shell',
// password_hash NULL) carrying a TeacherProfile with system_status='external'.
// That choice is load-bearing:
//   - every operational table already keys on the teacher's USER id
//     (courses/sessions/subscriptions/session_settlements/transactions), so
//     supporting them needed ZERO changes to any of those tables;
//   - joining the platform later is a flip of ONE column on the SAME id, so no
//     historical row ever moves and nothing can be lost in the conversion;
//   - "no login" is enforced by the EXISTING door (status must be 'active' and
//     a password hash must exist), not by a second parallel gate — same
//     reasoning as the ONE SUSPENSION MECHANISM rule.
enum TeacherSystemStatus {
  enrolled // uses the platform with their own account (every pre-existing teacher)
  external // off-system; the center keeps their records by manual entry

  @@map("teacher_system_status")
}

// How much a teacher's OWN account may do. `full` is every teacher, and today
// it is the only value anything writes.
//
// `read_only` is the MODEL HOOK the off-system work needed and nothing more:
// "the role model must tolerate giving an external teacher read-only access
// later". It is NOT written and NOT enforced anywhere yet — stated plainly
// because a column that claims a restriction nothing enforces is worse than no
// column at all. Taking a teacher off-system closes their login through
// `users.status` (the platform's one account gate, which fires session
// revocation); when read-only access is actually wanted, this column is where
// it goes, enforced in ONE place the way the center_accountant tier already is.
enum TeacherAccessLevel {
  full
  read_only

  @@map("teacher_access_level")
}

// Where a row came from. `system` = written by the platform's own flows (every
// row that existed before this feature — hence the default). `manual` = typed
// in by center staff on behalf of an off-system teacher. It is a PROVENANCE
// label for the UI and reports; it never changes what a row MEANS, and no
// authorization decision reads it.
enum DataSource {
  system
  manual

  @@map("data_source")
}

